# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
@ev_cosecha
title: La cosecha
new-page: true
face-image: img/cards/ejido.jpg
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and apoyo_popular >= 35 and time >= f_ev_last + 2
priority: 3
frequency: 60
max-visits: 8
on-arrival: f_ev_last = time

= La cosecha

Where the water is deep the sierra feeds the war without being robbed to do it: the coffee harvest tithed by choice, a steer "lost" on paper, the sacks that appear at the edge of the camp with no name attached. This is the line between a guerrilla and a bandit — the bandit takes and the people inform; the rooted column is *given*, and the whole valley covers for it. The harvest is in. What you do with the offering tells the sierra what kind of army you are.

- @cosecha_recibir: Receive it as the gift it is — supply for the column, and the base confirmed. *(+comida, +parque)*
- @cosecha_pagar: Pay for it, though they refuse — leave what little money you have, so no one can ever say the guerrilla ate the poor. *(costs funds; +apoyo, +deep trust)*

@cosecha_recibir
on-arrival: {! Q.f_comida+=12; Q.f_parque+=4; Q.apoyo_popular+=2; !}

You take what is offered, the way it only moves for a movement the country has adopted — quietly, reliably, with a deniability the valley maintains on its own. The column eats. The base is not diminished by the giving; it is confirmed. You are being *kept*, and that is a status no operation wins and no amount of parque buys.

- @root: Continuar.

@cosecha_pagar
on-arrival: {! Q.f_comida+=8; Q.apoyo_popular+=6; Q.funds=(Q.funds||0)-2; if(Q.funds<0){Q.funds=0;} Q.sup_peasants+=2; !}

You leave the money though they push it back into your hands, because the whole war is a wager that you are different from every armed man who ever came down out of these mountains to take. Word of it travels faster than any communiqué: *they paid.* It is a small thing and it is the entire thesis — the sea deepens by an inch across the whole sierra, bought with coins you could not really spare.

- @root: Continuar.

