@ev_ajusticiamiento
title: El ajusticiamiento
new-page: true
face-image: img/guardias_blancas.jpg
subtitle: The Brigada's oldest and most corrosive power
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and f_cerco >= 40 and time >= f_ev_last + 3
priority: 4
frequency: 45
max-visits: 5
on-arrival: f_ev_last = time

= El ajusticiamiento

The base brings you a name and a rope. A cacique who has bled these villages for thirty years and just handed three of your people to the army; or an informer, caught, who fed the captain your last position. The Partido de los Pobres kept a whole brigade for this — the Brigada Campesina de *Ajusticiamiento*, the peasant combat brigade whose middle name was the killing of the ones the villages could no longer bear. It works: fear is real, and an informer dead informs no more. It also does the thing that killed more focos than the army ever did — it teaches the sierra that you, too, are men who kill in the dark, and it plants in your own ranks the seed of every future purge.

- @ajust_hacer: Carry it out. The village asked; the security of the column demands it; justice, here, wears no other face. *(security now; erodes the water; a debt of fear comes due)*
- @ajust_juzgar: Try him before the assembly instead — let the villages judge in the light, and make even this an act of the people, not the gun. *(slower, +apoyo, +legitimacy of the movement)*
- @ajust_perdonar: Spare him, expose him, and let him live marked. Refuse to become what you are fighting. *(risk; but the water runs cleaner)*

@ajust_hacer
on-arrival: {! Q.ajusticiamientos=(Q.ajusticiamientos||0)+1; Q.f_cerco-=8; if(Q.f_cerco<0){Q.f_cerco=0;} Q.apoyo_popular-=5; Q.paranoia=(Q.paranoia||8)+6; Q.f_moral-=2; !}

It is done at the edge of the village before dawn, and for a while it works exactly as promised: the informers go quiet, the caciques travel with guards, the immediate leak is stopped. But something changes in the column that morning that does not change back. The villages are a little more careful around you now — grateful, afraid, and careful, which is not the same as loving. And in the ranks the arithmetic of suspicion has been taught: if we killed him for what he might have done, who among us is next? Every foco that ate itself began with a morning like this one.

- @root: Continuar.

@ajust_juzgar
on-arrival: {! Q.apoyo_popular+=4; Q.sup_peasants+=2; Q.f_cerco-=4; if(Q.f_cerco<0){Q.f_cerco=0;} Q.zona_gobernada=1; !}

You do the harder thing: you make it the people's, not the gun's. The assembly hears the case in the open, the witnesses speak, the sentence — whatever it is — is theirs, and carried out as an act of a community governing itself for the first time in its history. It is slower and it is not always merciful, but it draws the line the whole revolution depends on: that the movement answers to the villages and not the other way around. The sierra learns that where you are, there is *law* again, of a kind it makes itself. That is worth more than any informer's silence.

- @root: Continuar.

@ajust_perdonar
on-arrival: {! Q.apoyo_popular+=3; Q.f_cerco+=6; if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} Q.f_moral+=2; !}

You mark him and let him live, and some of the column thinks you are a fool, and they may be right — a spared informer is a risk that walks around on two legs. But you did not come up into these mountains to become the thing in the palace, and a movement that kills its way to safety has already lost the argument it is making. The water runs a little cleaner for the mercy. The ring runs a little tighter for it too. Both bills are real; you chose which to pay.

- @root: Continuar.

