@ev_represalia
title: La represalia
new-page: true
face-image: img/camioneta.jpg
subtitle: The army punishes a village for you
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and f_cerco >= 45 and time >= f_reprisal_last + 4
priority: 6
frequency: 50
max-visits: 5
on-arrival: f_reprisal_last = time

= La represalia

They cannot find you, so they punish the ones who hide you. A village — El Quemado, or one just like it — is emptied at gunpoint because a lieutenant is certain it fed you, and he is right. The men are taken to the airbase with the runway that points at the sea. The granaries burn. It is the dirty war's logic, and it is also, if you have the stomach to see it, its central mistake: every village the army burns for you sends its survivors up the mountain looking for the people the army was punishing them for loving.

- @repr_vengar: Answer it. Hit the garrison that did it, hard and publicly, so the sierra sees the guerrilla makes them pay for touching the people. *(+desgaste, +legend, +apoyo — but the war escalates)*
- @repr_alejar: Take the column away from them. You are the reason the soldiers came; leave, and the punishment leaves with you. *(protects the village; -apoyo here, but the human thing)*
- @repr_defender: Stand between the village and the next sweep. Fight to protect the people who sheltered you, whatever it costs. *(costly firefight; the deepest water in the war)*

@repr_vengar
on-arrival: {! Q.f_desgaste+=8; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+3; Q.apoyo_popular+=6; Q.legitimidad_regimen-=3; Q.f_parque-=6; if(Q.f_parque<0){Q.f_parque=0;} Q.f_cerco+=12; if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} Q.represion+=3; !}

You make the garrison pay for it where everyone can see — a column of theirs broken on the road out, the message unmistakable: touch the people and the sierra answers. The villages, who have spent generations watching the army act with total impunity, watch you break it, and something shifts. The reprisal that was meant to isolate you has recruited for you. It has also told the army exactly where its enemy is, and the ring tightens to match the blow.

- @root: Continuar.

@repr_alejar
on-arrival: {! Q.apoyo_popular-=4; Q.f_cerco-=14; if(Q.f_cerco<0){Q.f_cerco=0;} Q.f_moral-=4; if(Q.col_prof<5){Q.col_prof+=1;} !}

You do the thing that costs you and saves them: you leave. You are the weather the soldiers followed here, and when you go the storm goes with you — the sweeps ease, the airbase trucks turn around, the village is left standing, emptied but alive. It costs you the ground and a piece of the column's heart, because leaving people who fed you feels exactly like the abandonment it partly is. But a guerrilla who gets villages destroyed to feel loyal is worth less than one who takes his war somewhere the poor will not pay for it.

- @root: Continuar.

@repr_defender
on-arrival: {! var _r=(Q.f_hombres*0.5)+(Q.f_moral*0.3)-40+(Math.random()*30-12); if(_r>=0){Q.apoyo_popular+=10;Q.f_desgaste+=6;Q.f_moral+=4;Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+2;}else{Q.apoyo_popular+=8;Q.f_hombres-=4;Q.f_moral-=4;Q.f_bajas+=4;Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+3;} Q.f_parque-=8; if(Q.f_parque<0){Q.f_parque=0;} Q.f_cerco+=10; if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} !}

You put the column between the village and the next sweep, which is the thing a people's army is *for* and the thing that gets people's armies killed. [? if f_moral >= 55 : The soldiers, who expected to burn an undefended hamlet, meet fire instead and pull back to think about it — and the village watches the guerrilla bleed for it, which is worth more than any manifesto. ?][? if f_moral < 55 : It is a hard, ugly fight and you do not win it cleanly; you hold long enough to get the people out, and you leave some of your own in the doing. ?] The deepest water in this whole war is drawn from a well like this one. So is the deepest debt: the sierra knows, now, that you will come.

- @root: Continuar.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
@ev_figueroa
title: El secuestro del senador
new-page: true
face-image: img/congreso.jpg
subtitle: 1974 — the act that made Lucio, and doomed him
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and f_hombres >= 20 and apoyo_popular >= 45 and year >= 1974 and f_figueroa = 0
priority: 5
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: f_figueroa = 1

= El secuestro del senador

The chance comes the way it came to Lucio: a senator — a rich man, a cacique of caciques, a candidate for governor — moves through the sierra with too little guard and too much confidence, and for a few days he is *takeable.* A kidnapping like this is the loudest thing a foco can do: ransom enough to arm the column for a year, the release of comrades from Lecumberri, and the spectacle of the state's own aristocracy held helpless by the people it despises. It is also, history is obliged to note, precisely the act that turned the full weight of the army onto the sierra de Atoyac and, within months, ended Lucio in a coffee grove called El Otatal. The reward is enormous. So is the size of the fist it invites.

- @fig_hacer: Take him. The ransom, the prisoners, the message — worth the storm it brings. *(+parque, +funds, frees comrades; a massive encirclement follows)*
- @fig_no: Let him pass. The column is not ready to be the most-wanted thing in Mexico, and a foco that survives is worth more than one that is famous. *(no gain; the ring stays where it is)*

@fig_hacer
on-arrival: {! Q.f_parque+=20; Q.funds=(Q.funds||0)+20; Q.presos=0; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+6; Q.legitimidad_regimen-=6; Q.f_cerco=90; Q.coronel_activo=1; Q.f_desgaste-=6; Q.intervencion_riesgo+=4; !}

You take him on a mountain road and hold him in a camp the army will spend a fortune failing to find, and for a season you are the most powerful poor man in Mexico. The ransom arms the column to the teeth; comrades walk out of Lecumberri; the corridos write themselves. And then the fist closes, exactly as it closed on Lucio — thousands of troops, the airbase working around the clock, the sierra de Atoyac turned into the most heavily hunted ground in the country. You bought a year of war in an afternoon. Now you have to survive having done it.

- @root: Continuar.

@fig_no
on-arrival: {! Q.f_moral+=2; !}

You let him ride out of the sierra with his confidence intact and his story untold, and half the column thinks you are too cautious by half. Maybe. But you have read how this story ends when it is written the loud way, and you would rather have a foco in a year than a legend in a coffin. The most-wanted man in Mexico is a poor place to be when you are also the hungriest. The chance passes. So, for now, does the storm.

- @root: Continuar.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
@ev_enlace
title: El enlace con la ciudad
new-page: true
face-image: img/charola.jpg
subtitle: A hand extended from the urban war
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and f_hombres >= 16 and time >= f_ev_last + 4 and f_enlace_foco = 0
priority: 4
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: f_enlace_foco = 1; f_ev_last = time

= El enlace con la ciudad

A stranger reaches the camp with the right password and a proposal. The urban comrades — the Liga's people, or what remains of the MAR's North-Korea-trained cadre — can move you what the sierra never will: clean weapons bought with expropriated money, false papers, medicine, a route to the coast and out. In exchange they want coordination — that when they act in Guadalajara or the capital, your war in the south moves too, so the state cannot concentrate on either. It is the synthesis Che preached and rarely achieved: the city and the sierra as one war. It is also an exposure, because every link is a thread the DFS can pull.

- @enlace_si: Take the link. Arms, papers, a way out, and a war on two fronts the army cannot fight at once. *(+parque, +intelligence, ties the tracks together — and shares the heat)*
- @enlace_no: Stay pure. The sierra's strength is that it owes the city nothing and can be betrayed by no one it has not met. *(no gain; but no new thread for the enemy to pull)*

@enlace_si
on-arrival: {! Q.f_parque+=12; Q.inteligencia+=6; Q.apoyo_popular+=2; Q.expediente=(Q.expediente||0)+8; Q.internac_armada=(Q.internac_armada||0)+1; !}

You take the hand, and for a while the sierra has things it has never had — real weapons, real papers, real medicine, and the knowledge that when the columns of the city move, the army in the south cannot simply turn its whole attention to you. The synthesis is real, and it is powerful, and it costs exactly what synthesis always costs a guerrilla: a thread now runs from your camp to a safehouse in a city, and threads like that have unravelled better movements than yours. Worth it. Probably. You will find out.

- @root: Continuar.

@enlace_no
on-arrival: {! Q.f_moral+=2; !}

You send the stranger back with thanks and nothing else. The sierra's oldest strength is that it is a world unto itself — it eats what it grows, arms itself from the enemy, and can be sold out by no one it has never met. The city's war is louder and better supplied and it is being rolled up, cell by cell, in exactly the way a network can be and a mountain cannot. You keep your war small, and slow, and yours. It is a real choice, with a real cost. So was the other one.

- @root: Continuar.
